     "faith"
    ],
    "source": "Joan of Arc to Dunois at Orléans, April 1429, in Dunois’s deposition of 1456, Quicherat, Procès, vol. 3, p. 6 (our translation). https://archive.org/details/procsdecondam03joanuoft"
   },
   {
    "text": "Do not doubt; the hour is ready when it pleases God.",
    "topics": [
     "patience",
     "faith"
    ],
    "source": "Joan of Arc to the duke of Alençon at Jargeau, June 1429, in his deposition of 1456, Quicherat, Procès, vol. 3, p. 96 (our translation). https://archive.org/details/procsdecondam03joanuoft"
   },
   {
    "text": "Work, and God will work.",
    "topics": [
     "faith",
     "courage"
    ],
    "source": "Joan of Arc to the duke of Alençon at Jargeau, June 1429, in his deposition of 1456, Quicherat, Procès, vol. 3, p. 96 (our translation). https://archive.org/details/procsdecondam03joanuoft"
   },
   {
    "text": "There is more in our Lord’s books than in yours.",
    "topics": [
     "wisdom",
     "truth"
    ],
    "source": "Joan of Arc on the clerics, in the deposition of Marguerite La Touroulde, 1456, Quicherat, Procès, vol. 3, p. 86 (our translation). https://archive.org/details/procsdecondam03joanuoft"
   },
   {
    "text": "Touch them yourselves; they will be as good from your touch as from mine.",
    "topics": [
     "humility"
    ],
    "source": "Joan of Arc to the women of Bourges who brought rosaries, in the deposition of Marguerite La Touroulde, 1456, Quicherat, Procès, vol. 3, p. 87 (our translation). https://archive.org/details/procsdecondam03joanuoft"
   },
   {
    "text": "I wish it pleased God, my creator, that I might now leave, laying down my arms, and go to serve my father and mother by keeping their sheep.",
